program            = 008_noreturn
area               = 10_declarations_and_types
description        = _Noreturn declaration and its effect on reachable code, with a function that genuinely never returns and an unreachable statement after the call site
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
NORETURN DESIGN. C11 makes it undefined behaviour for a function declared _Noreturn to return
to its caller, so this program is built so that it provably cannot happen. terminate_now is
declared _Noreturn, prints one line, and then calls exit. exit is itself declared _Noreturn --
hand-declared as _Noreturn void exit(int), because no header may be included -- so it never
returns, and therefore control never reaches the closing brace of terminate_now. There is no
return statement anywhere in terminate_now, and no path through it can fall off the end. The
_Noreturn contract is honoured absolutely rather than merely intended, and the sanitizer gate
independently confirms it: UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer instruments _Noreturn functions and
reports when one actually returns, so a clean sanitizer run is positive evidence rather than
just an absence of complaint.

MAIN HAS NO RETURN STATEMENT, AND THAT IS WELL DEFINED. main ends with the call to
terminate_now, followed by an unreachable printf, followed by the closing brace, with no
return. Because terminate_now terminates the process, control never reaches either the
unreachable printf or the end of main, so no value is ever required from main and no
indeterminate status can be produced. The process exit status is 0, supplied explicitly by
exit(0), which is a normal exit rather than a signal termination and is well inside the
permitted 0 to 125 range. The absence of the after_noreturn line from the expected output is
itself the assertion: it is the observable proof that the call did not return. A compiler that
generated a return path would print a fourth line and the divergence would be immediate.

REMAINING UB-FREEDOM ARGUMENT. Every object read is initialized: before is assigned from
reachable_probe(0) at its declaration, and reachable_probe adds one to its parameter with no
other state. All arithmetic is on small int values far from the int range edges, so there is no
signed overflow: the largest value computed is 2. No shift and no pointer arithmetic is
performed. No object is modified twice between sequence points, and no printf call receives
more than one side-effecting argument -- reachable_probe is pure and mutates nothing. There is
no aliasing violation and no uninitialized read. No padding byte is read, because the program
declares no aggregate at all.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This program prints no size and no alignment at all, so the measured i686 width differences
(4-byte long and pointer versus 8 bytes on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64) cannot surface. All
printed values are small int quantities. No address or pointer value is printed. Plain char is
not used, so the measured char signedness difference (signed on x86_64 and i686, unsigned on
aarch64 and riscv64) is irrelevant. The only printf conversion specifier used in the program is
%d, and it appears three times, the fewest of any program in this area.

KEYWORD SPELLING. The lowercase noreturn macro lives in the bundled header stdnoreturn.h, which
this program does not include, so the C11 keyword _Noreturn is used directly on both the
hand-declared exit prototype and the terminate_now definition. _Noreturn is documented as one
of the supported C11 keywords. Hand-declaring a libc prototype is the corpus-wide technique and
is not the same thing as including a header: bcc ships no stdio.h and no stdlib.h, so an
include of either would fail against bcc while succeeding against the reference compiler and
would manufacture a divergence caused by the test rather than by the compiler.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
before=1
reachable=2
noreturn_reached=1 code=0
END
